{
  "schema_version": 1.0,
  "name": "The Long March",
  "description": "A wide deep river runs the full length of the map. A single causeway bridges it near the south; small islands in the center hold the only high-yield metal; shallow fords at the extreme north and south are the slow alternative. The banks rise 12-18m above the river bed on long ridges, so the crossing is a real descent. Whoever controls the causeway and the central island controls the river crossing.",
